{
  "_comment": "Section 5 experimental corpus for the C0-C3 runtime-verification sweep. 80 cases across 6 categories, grounded directly in the real action/parameter set defined in behavior_schema.py (not invented). Instructions are Korean, matching voice_control_go2.KOREAN_SYSTEM_PROMPT. expect_reject is a best-effort label based on what the current, real implementation is expected to do -- for a few cases (see 'note' field) this deliberately encodes a known inconsistency/limitation in the real code rather than an idealized 'correct' answer, because that gap is itself part of what Section 6/7 report. The LLM's actual output is not fully deterministic (temperature=0.3 in run_verification_benchmark.py), so treat expect_reject as an analysis aid, not ground truth -- the harness records what actually happened per layer.",
  "_live_subset_note": "40 of the 80 cases are marked \"live_candidate\": true, selected (not randomly, to maximize coverage of distinct actions/parameters/injection patterns within the physical-trial time budget) as 8 per category from the 5 non-contextual categories (benign, invalid_action, invalid_parameter, conflicting_instruction, injected_instruction). Run with: python run_verification_benchmark.py --live --configs C0 C3 --live-subset-only. Per-layer latency numbers (schema_ms/intent_ms/context_ms) do not depend on live vs dry-run, so C1/C2 are not re-run physically -- only C0 (baseline) vs C3 (full protection) are, to keep the physical/battery/time budget on the strongest before/after contrast. The contextual_safety category is intentionally excluded from this corpus-based live subset: run_verification_benchmark.py's _build_robot_state() overrides a RobotState object directly rather than reading real telemetry, so a live C0 trial on one of these cases would execute on the physical robot using a *simulated* battery/obstacle value that need not match the robot's real state at that moment. The paper's live evaluation of context-aware gating instead uses a separately staged case study (~10-15 trials) where battery/obstacle conditions are genuinely physically true at trial time, not injected.",
